feat(audit): mirror logAdminAction into unified audit_log table

Roadmap item 14 (partial — admin-side routes already call logAdminAction;
this commit threads them through audit_log so the DB-Editor audit pane
sees them too).

backend/src/lib/audit.ts → logAdminAction()
  - Existing adminActions insert preserved as primary (legacy Activity
    Log UI still reads from there).
  - New: mirror every call to audit_log via recordAudit(), with the
    optional meta = { ip, target, success } passed through to the
    unified record.
  - Both writes are independent try/catch — a failure in one doesn't
    poison the other (audit logging never breaks the action it records).

Optional meta param is backward-compatible: every existing call site
keeps working without changes. Routes that want to surface IP/target
in the unified pane can opt in at their leisure.

Why mirror instead of refactor everything onto recordAudit?
  - Switching the legacy Activity Log UI is a separate concern.
  - adminActions has its own pagination/search shaped for that UI;
    audit_log is shaped for SQL-style filtering.
  - Two tables, one write call — small redundancy cost, no risk of
    breaking the legacy admin dashboard.

Build: 510 modules. 80/80 lib tests pass.